  "body": "## What changed\n\nWhen a launcher was running, the Windows installer deferred the update and printed only a short \"staged\" notice — losing the command reference that a Linux/WSL install shows. The full mcc message (start the proxy, use a coding agent, manage/inspect, legacy aliases, restart note) now prints on both paths.\n\nExtracted `Write-MccCommandReference` and call it from:\n- the direct-install success message, and\n- the deferred (app running) path inside `Start-DeferredInstall`.\n\nSo Windows and WSL/Linux show the same content after install. The staging notice still leads before the reference in the deferred case.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Scriptblock-form install with a running launcher now prints the full mcc command reference after the staging notice:\n  ```\n  My Claude Code is currently running. The update to v5.1.1 is staged and\n  will complete after you stop the running app, then restart it (mcc-server).\n  The new version is picked up on restart.\n\n  Start the proxy:\n    mcc-server              Start the local proxy and admin dashboard\n  ...\n  Update staged for after restart.\n  ```\n- Static test asserts the shared function is called from both paths.\n- `ruff`/`ty` clean. Full suite: **16 failed / 3663 passed** — identical failure set to unmodified main (16 pre-existing PowerShell failures), zero regressions.\n\n## Residual risks\n\n- None beyond the documented pre-existing PowerShell installer/uninstaller failures (environmental, identical on main).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
