    "message": "fix: 5.1.2 Windows installer shows the same mcc command reference as WSL\n\nWhen a launcher was running, the Windows installer deferred the update and\nprinted only a short \"staged\" notice, losing the command reference that a\nLinux/WSL install shows. The full mcc message (start the proxy, use a coding\nagent, manage/inspect, legacy aliases, restart note) now prints on both paths.\n\nExtracted Write-MccCommandReference and call it from the direct-install success\nmessage and the deferred (app running) path, so Windows and WSL/Linux show the\nsame content after install. The staging notice still leads before the reference\nin the deferred case.\n\nVerified: scriptblock-form install with a running launcher now prints the full\nmcc command reference after the staging notice. Static test asserts the shared\nfunction is called from both paths. ruff/ty clean. Full suite 16 failed / 3663\npassed -- identical failure set to unmodified main, zero regressions.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
